titre $Laccaria Vellinga
com$ FLORA AGARICINA NEERLANDICA 3 pp 96-103  / adapt GF dec 2010
1,2 $Basidiocarp with violet or purple(-brown) tinges, either in fruitbody as a whole, or only in young lamellae and basal tomentum.
1,4 $Basidiocarp pinkish, buff, pinkish brown, red-brown etc.; sometimes with violet tinges in context in base of stipe or in old lamellae.
1,0$ NB : les numéros devant les noms d'espèce renvoient à la description dans l'ouvrage.
2,0 $Pileus and stipe brown, lamellae when young lilac, pink with age; basal tomentum and sometimes basal part of stipe pale violet. $3 L. bicolor
2,3 $Basidiocarp completely violet, amethyst or purple-brown.
3,0 $Basidiocarp amethyst-coloured; exsiccate pale amethyst ochre yellowish; spores globose to broadly ellipsoid ( Q= 1.0-1.1) with 1.0-1.5 µm high spines $7 L. amethystina
3,0 $Basidiocarp purple-brown; exsiccate pinkish purple-brown; spores broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid ( Q=1.25-1.35) with c. 0.5µm  highspines. $8 L. purpureobadia
4,0 $Surface of pileus slightly viscous; hyphae of pileipellis slightly gelatinized; spores large, oblong to cylindrical with low spines up to 0.5 µm high, nearly glabrous; habitat in drift sand dunes along the coast. $9 L. maritima
4,5 $Surface of pileus dry and hyphae of pileipelIis not gelatinized; spores globose to ellipsoid with 0.5-2.5 µm high spines all over; habitat not in drift sanddunes along the coast, though occasionally in Salix repens scrub.
5,6 $Basidia mainly ( > 2,.0 %) 2-sored.
5,8 $Basidia mainly ( > 90 %) 4-spored.
6,0 $Spores globose ( Q=0.95-1.0), 10-15 µm in diameter with high up to 2.5µm  conical spines $6 L. tortilis
6,7 $Spores 9.0-12.5 µm long, globose to ellipsoid ( Q= 1.1-1.2) with spines 0.5-1.0 (-1.3) µm high.
7,0 $Pileus orange-brown or reddish brown, small (7-26 mm), concolorous with stipe, translucently striate up to centre. $4 L. pumila
7,0 $Pileus red-brown to purplish brown, medium-sized (10-)18-39 mm , translucently striate up to 112 of radius; stipe darker to concolorous $5 L. fraterna
8,9 $Spores broadly ellipsoid to ellipsoid ( Q= 1.2-1.35).
8,11$Spores globo se to broadly ellipsoid, rarely ellipsoid ( Q= 1.0-1.25).
9,0 $Basidiocarp purplish brown with coarsely striate stipe " $8 L. purpureobadia
9,10 $Basidiocarp with brownish, orange-brown, pink-brown tinges, with or without coarsely striate stipe.
10,0 $Basidiocarp with a combination of orange-brown, squamulose pileus, pale coloured lamellae when young, and a coarsely brown with cream striate stipe '- $2 L. proxima
10,0 $Pileus with buff to brown tinges, not really dark orange-brown, glabrous, rarely squamulose, only more squamose on drying; lamellae pink when young; stipe uniformly coloured with hyaline striation.. $1 L. Iaccata var. laccata 
10,0,n$ not yet recorded from the Netherlands, only known from Sweden 
